- `quit_does_not_fire_on_unterminated_if` — `if x > 0\n    y = 1;\n` → no QUIT
- `quit_does_not_fire_on_incomplete_tail` — `x = 1; 2` → no QUIT (EOFMI fires)

## Pitfalls
- The panic guard must discard partial diagnostics and return only QUIT.
- Verify `Linter::lint`'s actual signature/return type in linter.rs before editing.
- QUIT is not a registry rule → cannot be muted by config (honors can_be_disabled=false).
- Existing EOFER/EOFMI/ENDCT/SYNER/TMSMS tests must stay green.

